Report the position of a DFT pen from the MPP v2 position windows (ExtraPositionWindows)

An MPP v2 pen sends its tip tone in several windows of a group, and every window is sampled at
its own time. On the Surface Pro 9 with the Slim Pen 2 the position window (0x06, 25 kHz tone)
is followed by the two MPP v2 position windows 2.9 ms (0x07) and 10.1 ms (0x08) later in a 15 ms
frame; their tip tone is about 15 times stronger. Measured on the device: their positions lie on
one path when ordered by the window timestamps (median distance 0.01 to 0.03 mm), while the
position of the 0x06 window is off by up to 1.7 mm when the pen is tilted.

With [DFT] ExtraPositionWindows the position is taken from the 0x07 and 0x08 windows and a sample
is emitted for each: 133 samples per second instead of 67, 7.2 and 7.8 ms apart. The 0x06 window
still decides proximity and lift and its sample is still what announces them; a sample from the
other windows is only emitted while the 0x06 window of the same group found the pen. While those
samples flow, the 0x06 position is not reported (alternating between the two makes the path
zigzag); if a group delivers none, the next 0x06 window reports as before. Off by default, and
without these windows nothing changes.

